  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">C&#xf4;te d&apos;Ivoire Net-Zero Nature-Positive Integrated Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The objective of the GEF PPG is to develop the project concept into a full project: C&#xf4;te dIvoire Net-Zero Nature-Positive Integrated Program. As described in the project concept (PIF/child project concept note), this project aims to support C&#xf4;te dIvoire in its transition towards net-zero emissions and a positive trajectory for nature. It will address climate challenges at both the national and territorial levels by involving all categories of territorial communities in C&#xf4;te dIvoire. It will be implemented in three autonomous districts (Dengu&#xe9;l&#xe9;, Montagne, Valle Bandama) and five regions (Haut-Sassandra, Nawa, La M&#xe9;, Gontougo, Bago&#xe9;) of the country, which face systemic challenges such as poverty, gender inequality, limited access to basic services, the rise of violent extremism, and illegal immigration. The Haut-Sassandra region (Daloa) has become a hub for departures to Europe.</narrative>
  </description>
